Oscar_MEGA65_r3_r6
==================

Oscar_MEGA65_r3_r6 is an original FPGA implementation of Data East's
Psycho-Nics Oscar, developed for the MEGA65 by Muse.

This is not a port of an existing Jotego Oscar core. The implementation
uses reusable components from Jotego's JTFRAME/JTCORES framework,
including video and arcade hardware building blocks.

  * JTFRAME / JTCORES by Jose Tejada (Jotego) and contributors
    https://github.com/jotego/jtcores

Other than that and my own work, Oscar_MEGA65_r3_r6 uses:
---------------------------------------------------------

  * T65 65xx-compatible CPU core, originally developed by Daniel Wallner,
    with contributions from Mike Johnson, Wolfgang Scherr and Morten Leikvoll.
    The version used also contains subsequent fixes by other contributors.
    https://opencores.org/projects/t65
    https://github.com/mist-devel/T65

  * MiSTer2MEGA65 by The MiSTer2MEGA65 Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/MiSTer2MEGA65

  * QNICE Co-Processor and System-on-a-Chip for file operations and
    on-screen menu by The QNICE Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/QNICE-FPGA

  * Various MEGA65 drivers taken from the MEGA65 VHDL source by
    Paul Gardner-Stephen and contributors
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-core

  * VGA Timing Generator by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=15925278

  * VGA to HDMI converter IP core by Adam Barnes
    https://github.com/amb5l/tyto_project

  * AVALON SCALER used for scaling to 720p for HDMI by temlib.org
    http://temlib.org/site/?page_id=10

  * HyperRAM controller by MJoergen
    https://mjoergen.github.io/HyperRAM/

  * Debouncer: I/O debouncing used for the joysticks by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=4980758

  * Anikki-16x16 font, archived and provided by k80w
    https://github.com/k80w/consolefonts

  * PSF font to text file converter nafe-0.1 by Corvus Corax
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/nafe/

  * PSF font to C include file converter psftools-1.1.1 by John Elliott
    https://www.seasip.info/Unix/PSF/

The T65 CPU core carries its own copyright and redistribution conditions.
Retain the original copyright and licence notices in its source files,
and comply with its licence when distributing source or synthesized builds.
